# 0001. Record architecture decisions as .adr files

- Status: Proposed
- Date: 2026-11-19

Decisions with long-term consequences for this config are recorded as numbered `.adr` files
in `docs/adr/`, so the why is in one place, like the nvim and zsh repos.

## Technical details
- **Problem**: the reasons behind the config lived in comments, README "Notes", `CLAUDE.md`
  conventions and PR bodies; nvim and zsh already keep ADRs, tmux didn't.
- **Files**: `docs/adr/NNNN-short-title.adr`: sequential four-digit numbers, never reused;
  Markdown content with the `.adr` extension. `docs/adr/README.md` is the index.
- **Format**: the `adr-manager` template (title, Status, Date, purpose, Technical details,
  Technologies and alternatives). Statuses: Proposed, Accepted, Rejected, Deprecated,
  Superseded (linked both ways).
- **History**: 0002-0007 are recorded retroactively from the code, README, `CLAUDE.md`,
  `CHANGELOG.md` and the commits `628f797`, `5e17e96` (#1), `9d54876` (#2).
- **Commits**: subjects carry the ADR they fall under (`[ADR-NNNN]`, minor `[ADR-NNNN.N]`,
  `commit-style`); `CLAUDE.md` says to read the ADR before changing a recorded decision.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Alternatives: keep the why in README/`CLAUDE.md`: mixed with usage docs, no status or
  supersession; `.md` extension: ADRs can't be told apart from other docs.
